### Schema
```graphql
  extend type Subscription {
    CurrentTagNotifications(
      userId: Int
      organizationId: Int
    ): [CurrentTagNotification!]!
  }
```
I know what you're going to say, why not yield individual `CurrentTagNotification`s?  But that would destroy performance of my UI; I need to send changes in bulk and update the client-side cache in bulk.  So if arrays don't work here (GraphQL better support this) the ugly workaround is to unnecessarily wrap with an object.
